rehearsal.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Believing that more rehearsals without any change will fix problems. Rehearsal works best when each run has one clear focus and one improvement. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating rehearsal on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with rehearsal, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Strong answer: ''Hold the final shape for three counts and look at the audience. I will rehearse again and ask them if the end is clear.'' A held final shape… This matches the lesson skill for rehearsal.","options":["Strong answer: ''Hold the final shape for three counts and look at the audience. I will rehearse again and ask them if the end is clear.'' A held final shape…","Believing that more rehearsals without any change will fix problems. Rehearsal works best when each run has one clear focus and one improvement.","Say it looks nice with no element or technique named.","Copy the example artwork or script and call that independent work."],"question":"After a rehearsal, your viewer says they could not tell when the dance ended. Write one change and say how you will check that it worked. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Believing that more rehearsals without any change will fix problems. Rehearsal works best when each run has one clear focus and one improvement. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson ide